  "title": "Objective Dysgraphia Detection via Deep Learning Frameworks",
  "summary": "This paper introduces a multi-branch deep learning framework for objective dysgraphia detection using online handwriting data, leveraging complementary image and signal-based representations. It evaluates the fusion of GAF, MOMENT, and handcrafted kinematic features to outperform individual representations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The framework uses two complementary branches to extract handcrafted and embedding-based kinematic features from raw temporal signals.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The four representations were evaluated on the publicly available DiaGraMo dataset, showing superior performance over individual and joint fusion schemes.",
